  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1410.01 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1410.01 Applicability.\n\n(a) Except as provided in (b), below, this part shall apply to used oil fuel marketers.\n\n(b) The following persons shall not be considered used oil fuel marketers subject to this part:\n\n(1) A used oil generator, household DIY used oil collection center, commercial used oil collection center, or used oil aggregation point, or a used oil transporter that transports used oil received only from such entities, that directs a shipment of used oil to a used oil processor/re-refiner that incidentally burns used oil as described in Env-Hw 1409.01(b)(2);\n\n(2) A person who directs shipments of on-specification used oil and who is not the first person to claim the oil meets the used oil fuel specifications of Env-Hw 1404.02; and\n\n(3) A used oil generator, or the owner or operator of a household DIY used oil collection center, commercial used oil collection center, or used oil aggregation point, that:\n\na. Tests and burns used oil onsite in compliance with Env-Hw 1406.04; or\n\nb. Directs used oil to a used oil burner that has notified and operates as a used oil fuel marketer under this part.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
